<!--Post: 110--><!--Time: 1085730872-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST110"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 28, 2004 - 12:54 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m aware the &#34;WSU connection&#34; has been discussed before, but here&#39;s another perspective: <BR> <BR>BTK: &#34;Haven&#39;t I seen you at the university?&#34; <BR>Those words were directed at Kevin Bright, a man BTK intended to kill. Dead men tell no tales and BTK probably didn&#39;t think twice about revealing such a clue. I believe those words are proof BTK was at WSU on a regular basis. <BR> <BR>A BTK letter sent to the news media was determined to have been copied from the university library. How likely is it that BTK felt such a match could ever be made to that particular copy machine? Not very. Therefore, I believe BTK chose that copier because of its easy access and because of his level of comfort in that location due to familiarity. <BR> <BR>BTK: &#34;That is correct.&#34; <BR>Those words were directed at a police dispatcher after BTK reported the Nancy Fox homicide. Most people use contractions when they speak and would have instead said, &#34;That&#39;s correct.&#34;  <BR> <BR>BTK&#39;s speech pattern was methodical, polished and confident. He pronounced his words perfectly. <BR> <BR>Being in his late 20s/early 30s during the mid-to-late 1970s would tend to rule out BTK as a WSU student. However, I believe BTK&#39;s own words rule him in as a member of the WSU faculty. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 110-->
<!--Post: 111--><!--Time: 1085763441-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST111"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitaboy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitaboy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 28, 2004 - 9:57 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK said to Kevin Bright, &#34;Haven&#39;t I seen you at the university?”   <BR> <BR>I believe that BTK said, “Haven’t I seen you at The University?” <BR> <BR>The distinction is that BTK meant The University Pub on 17th Street not WSU!  <BR> <BR>In the vernacular of the time, if you were talking about the college you would say WSU.  If you were referring to The University Pub, it would be The University.  That way there would be no misunderstanding about where you were talking about.  I believe that BTK asked, “Haven’t I seen you at The University?” because that is a bar that he frequented.   <BR> <BR>During the 70s The University Pub was a popular hang out for students and non-students in the under 30 crowd.  The University had a great lunch crowd.  There would be parties every night, pool tournaments, free pitchers for the ladies, etc.  A gentleman who worked for The Wichita Eagle-Beacon owned the University.  Because of the ownership of the bar, you could always see Eagle-Beacon employees there.  I believe that BTK frequented that bar in the 70s.  He was probably even friendly with some of the newspaper people.  <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 111-->
<!--Post: 112--><!--Time: 1085770789-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST112"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 28, 2004 - 11:59 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Wichitaboy wrote: <BR>&#34;The distinction is that BTK meant The University Pub on 17th Street not WSU!&#34; <BR> <BR>Well, only BTK knows for sure. <BR> <BR>What we know for sure is that BTK spent time on the WSU campus. So far, there&#39;s no evidence he ever set foot in any pub.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 112-->
<!--Post: 119--><!--Time: 1085783476-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST119"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Juno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Juno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 28, 2004 - 3:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think that he may have been more likely to say &#34;on campus&#34; if he meant WSU.  <BR> <BR>There was a bar just off north campus at OSU called &#34;The Library.&#34; <BR> <BR>Anyway, as far as BTK goes,I would guess faculty, grad student or security/campus police.  Definite WSU connection---I agree with that 100% Tom. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 119-->
<!--Post: 123--><!--Time: 1085788081-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST123"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:deltadawn194531@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Sandy<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sandy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 28, 2004 - 4:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK seems to have a formal way of speaking,so for him to say at the University,I think it would fit his way of speaking. Whats interesting about the University Pub is,I read on another site about a man back in the mid 70&#39;s who didn&#39;t seem to fit in with the rest of the crowd. This man was older than most of the people,and stood around just observing the people not speaking to anyone at a pub.Anyone know if that was the same pub?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 123-->
<!--Post: 163--><!--Time: 1086257635-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST163"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Unsub<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Unsub<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, June 03, 2004 - 3:13 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Someone from that area who attended the school said that it was normal for faculty to refer to it as the university but not for the students to do so. As for age, if he was ex-military that could add some years, he could also have been a gradute student. Along those lines maybe he was a gradute student and a TA so he was faculty but not a professor. He longest gap between killings was 9 years, I looked at a school near me and that was the time frame one had to do a Phd, start to finish<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 163-->
<!--Post: 183--><!--Time: 1086336198-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST183"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->J_eric<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->J_eric<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, June 04, 2004 - 1:03 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;Haven&#39;t I seen you...&#34; sounds like a generic pick-up line, useful in any large city from Boston to Berkeley.  It could mean BTK was a traveller, student or mere visitor to Wichita. That also might explain his long &#34;absence&#34; from that town; he went elsewhere, to lead a &#34;normal&#34; life or try out his deadly lines in a new locale...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 183-->
<!--Post: 353--><!--Time: 1088311507-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST353"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Matt<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Matt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, June 26, 2004 - 9:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In reference to WSU Campus Police; In about 1986 or 1987, a five year old girl named Amanda Schaefer was kidnapped from a mobile home park on West Kellogg, close to Goddard.  She was last seen riding her bicycle in the mobile home park.  The Sheriff&#39;s Dept. searched for her all that afternoon and evening, interviewing everyone who lived there.  One of the people living there was a campus Police Officer.  Amanda&#39;s nude, strangled body was found in a roadside ditch about a mile and a half away the next day by two Sedgwick County Highway Dept. employees.  All possible leads were followed, even going out to California to interview a known child molester who left the Mobile Home Park that week for California. <BR> <BR>About four years later, the case was closed when the murderer turned himself in.  He was at that time a former  campus security officer. He did go to prison on a plea bargain.  I don&#39;t know when he got out.  Maybe recently?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 353-->
<!--Post: 354--><!--Time: 1088312311-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST354"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Matt<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Matt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, June 26, 2004 - 9:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->About the line &#34;Haven&#39;t I seen you at the University&#34;? directed towards Kevin Bright. At that time, Kevin Bright was under eighteen, and not old enough to go to the University Pub.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 354-->
<!--Post: 357--><!--Time: 1088402508-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST357"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, June 27, 2004 - 11:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hmm... kinda rules that theory out then.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 357-->
<!--Post: 373--><!--Time: 1088636224-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST373"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Matt<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Matt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, June 30, 2004 - 3:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In reference to my message of 6/26- I neglected to mention the killer lived in Amanda&#39;s mobile home park, and she was in his trailer when the park was being searched.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 373-->
